  { q: 'How long does it take to form an LLC in Washington?', a: 'Online Certificate of Formation filings are usually processed by the Secretary of State within a few business days. Your business license from the Department of Revenue follows after that. Expedited state processing is available for an extra fee.' },
  { q: 'Can I form a Washington LLC myself?', a: 'Yes. You can file the Certificate of Formation with the Secretary of State and the Business License Application with the Department of Revenue yourself. Many owners hire a service to avoid mistakes and save time, since the steps are split between two state agencies and the IRS.' },
  { q: 'Do I need an operating agreement in Washington?', a: 'Washington does not require you to file one with the state, but every LLC should have one. It sets out who owns the company, how decisions are made and what happens if an owner leaves. Banks often ask for it when you open an account.' },
  { q: 'Is a Washington LLC the same as a business license?', a: 'No. The LLC is created by the Secretary of State. Your business license comes from the Department of Revenue and lets you legally operate and register for state taxes. Most Washington LLCs need both.' },
];
